CHAPTER II

RIGHTS OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 5 Every woman victim of violence has the right:
a. to have her dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;
c. to physical, psychological and sexual health recovery in accordance with the suffering experienced by Women Victims of Violence;
d. to special handling related to the confidentiality of Women Victims of Violence;
e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to spiritual guidance services; and g. to make her own decisions.

Part Five

Article 16

1. SPM in the field of integrated services for women and children victims of violence aims to ensure that Women Victims of violence receive the minimum services needed.
2. SPM in the field of integrated services for Women Victims of violence includes services for:a. handling complaints/reports of Victims of Violence Against Women;
b. health services for women Victims of violence; c. social rehabilitation for women Victims of violence;
d. law enforcement and Legal Aid for women Victims of violence;
e. Repatriation and Social Reintegration for women Victims of violence; and f. in the event that a Woman Victim of Violence experiences trauma or illness that endangers herself as a result of acts of violence requiring immediate assistance, the Regional Government is obliged to provide first aid no later than 7 (seven) days after the complaint is filed.

Article 17 (1) SPM as referred to in Article 16 has performance indicators including:
a. coverage of women victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in integrated Service units;
b. coverage ...

Paragraph 1

Article 12

1. In supporting the implementation of the Protection of Women, the Regent establishes PPT.
2. PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:a. UPTD PPA;
b. hospital-based PPT;
c. sub-district PPT; and d. Village/kelurahan PPT.
3. Further provisions regarding the procedures for establishing PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 13 ( 1) PPT Services include:
a. providing Services and handling as quickly as possible to Women Victims of Violence;
b. providing ...

